{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Surface\nAWS CloudWatch, region us-east-1, account 896586841071, host `rebar-gerrit` (rebar-autodeploy.service).\n\n## Signature (three correlated `rebar/host` autodeploy alarms flapped in-window)\n1. **rebar-autodeploy-errors** — `deploy_errors` (AUTODEPLOY_ERROR markers): **11** OK→ALARM transitions in window; currently OK (recovered 2026-08-30T17:32 PDT). Deploy is fail-safe (last-known-good stays live) but a sustained signal = `main` not reaching the box.\n2. **rebar-autodeploy-mcp-retire-cap** — `mcp_retire_cap`: **11** OK→ALARM transitions; currently OK (recovered 2026-08-30T03:12 PDT). Blue/green port-pool cap hit — retiring mcp containers not draining, new releases back off.\n3. **rebar-autodeploy-review-interrupts-signal-unavailable** — `review_interrupts_signal_unavailable`: **2** OK→ALARM (2026-08-30T16:53 PDT, cleared 17:08). The review-bot `/health` `in_flight` drain check could not be read, so a deploy recreated the review-bot with NO drain check (the silent regression bug 34cd exists to catch).\n\n## Root cause (proven — see the RCA comment on this ticket)\n**Mechanism 1 (deploy_errors ×11 + mcp-retire-cap ×11 — same event).** `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` sets uvicorn `timeout_graceful_shutdown=int(grace_seconds)` (line 743) where `grace_seconds` defaults to the 1200s certified-op drain budget `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS` (line 51), and `make_sigterm_handler` sets `server.should_exit=True` **before** draining the in-flight gauge. For a Streamable-HTTP MCP server, connected clients hold long-lived streams, so uvicorn's graceful shutdown then waits the FULL 1200s for those idle held-open streams even when the certified-op gauge is already 0. With only two blue-green rotation ports (8092/8093), a retiring container pins a port ~20 min → the next mcp deploy hits `port-exhausted` → `deploy_failed` + backoff. A high-cadence landing burst (14 mcp deploys + 142 bot redeploys in-window) drove this 11×. Origin: commit `8297083532a3` (`rebar-ticket: fd4a-4e91-f179-4932`); design-limitation record reopened as `40a7`.\n\n**Mechanism 3 (review-interrupts signal-unavailable ×2).** In `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` the drain gate reads the bot's `/health` `in_flight`; on an unreadable/unreachable signal `bot_in_flight_reviews()` returns `-1` and the gate **fails open** — it recreates the review-bot with no drain check and emits `AUTODEPLOY_REVIEW_INTERRUPT signal-unavailable`. It cannot distinguish a bot that is **mid-redeploy** (unreachable only because it is itself being recreated / still starting) from a bot that is genuinely **wedged**. In the mid-redeploy case the blind recreate re-enters the same window and can kill the very startup it should wait for.\n\n## Approach\nTwo independent, bounded, reversible fixes; each covered by its own RED→GREEN test.\n\n**Fix 1 — decouple uvicorn graceful-shutdown from the certified-op grace (`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py`).**\n- Add a short module constant `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS` (a few seconds) and use it for `uvicorn.Config(timeout_graceful_shutdown=...)`, DECOUPLED from `grace_seconds` (which stays the certified-op drain budget). Thread it as a defaulted `uvicorn_graceful_seconds` parameter to `run_http_with_grace` for testability.\n- Reorder `make_sigterm_handler`'s `_on_sigterm` to **drain the in-flight gauge FIRST** (via the existing `drain_then_exit`, bounded by `grace_seconds`), and only set `server.should_exit=True` AFTER the gauge reaches 0. While a real certified op is in flight, uvicorn keeps serving so the op's streaming response completes normally; once the gauge is 0, uvicorn's short backstop sweeps idle held-open streams in seconds instead of burning the full 1200s.\n- **Invariant preserved:** a container with >0 in-flight certified ops still gets the full `grace_seconds` drain (never cut a real op short); only a 0-in-flight container drains fast. The certified-op bound is enforced entirely by the gauge poll, never by uvicorn's (now short) backstop.\n\n**Fix 3 — distinguish \"bot mid-redeploy\" from \"bot wedged\" before failing open (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`).**\n- Add a best-effort, host-observable `bot_unreachable_disposition()` that inspects the review-bot container's docker state/health and echoes `redeploying` (container `restarting`/`created`/`removing`/`paused`, or docker health `starting`) vs `wedged` (running-but-unreachable, `unhealthy`, no container, or any inspect error → default `wedged`).\n- In the drain gate's `inflight < 0` branch, when the disposition is `redeploying`, **DEFER** (retry on the next timer tick) with a distinct countable marker `AUTODEPLOY_DEFERRED bot-redeploying`, bounded by the existing `DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX` episode so a bot that never finishes starting cannot freeze the gate; on bound-exhaustion (or a `wedged` disposition) fall through to the existing fail-open recreate + `signal-unavailable` marker. This maps the single unknown (`-1`) onto its own disposition instead of a blind fail-open (mirrors the 1c0d disposition-contract intent).\n- **Invariant preserved:** a genuinely wedged/down bot still fails open and deploys (the recovery path), and the mid-redeploy defer is bounded so it can never live-lock the gate. The safe default on any docker error is `wedged` (== pre-fix behavior).\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` — Fix 1 (new constant, `run_http_with_grace` param + Config, `make_sigterm_handler` reorder + docstrings). No change to `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS` (still 1200), the gauge, or `drain_then_exit`.\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` — Fix 3 (new `bot_unreachable_disposition()`; drain-gate `inflight < 0` branch). No change to the `inflight > 0` busy-defer path, the port pool, or `MCP_RELEASES_CAP` (Option 2 capacity is explicitly DEFERRED, not touched).\n- Tests only otherwise.\n- **Out of scope / deferred:** raising `MCP_RELEASES_CAP` / expanding the blue-green port pool (Option 2); any nginx/compose/infra capacity change; the separate concurrent disk bug e4f3.\n\n## Testing\n- **Fix 1** (`tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py`): a test that `make_sigterm_handler` does NOT set `should_exit` while the gauge is >0 and only flips it after the gauge drains to 0 (fast-drain + the >0-in-flight full-grace preservation guard); and a test that `run_http_with_grace` configures `timeout_graceful_shutdown` to the short `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS`, decoupled from (and less than) the 1200s op grace. The existing bound/exit tests continue to pass.\n- **Fix 3** (`tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py`, real-bash stub harness): a mid-redeploy bot (unreachable `/health` + docker state `starting`) is DEFERRED (no `compose build/up`, `AUTODEPLOY_DEFERRED bot-redeploying` emitted, no `signal-unavailable`, deployed-sha unchanged, rc 0); a wedged bot (unreachable + docker state `running`) still fails open (`compose build` runs, `signal-unavailable` counted); the mid-redeploy defer is bounded (a pre-aged episode past `DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX` falls through to fail-open).\n- `make lint` + `make typecheck` + the two targeted test modules; mutation check with teeth on the changed logic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n1. A retiring MCP container with **0** in-flight certified ops shuts down within the short `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS` backstop (not the 1200s op grace), so a held session no longer pins a blue-green port for ~20 min — removing the `mcp-retire-cap port-exhausted` / `deploy_failed` recurrence at normal landing cadence.\n2. A retiring MCP container with **>0** in-flight certified ops still receives the full `grace_seconds` drain and is never cut short (invariant proven by test).\n3. When the review-bot `/health` signal is unreadable because the bot is **mid-redeploy**, autodeploy DEFERS (bounded) with a countable `AUTODEPLOY_DEFERRED bot-redeploying` marker instead of blindly recreating the bot and emitting `signal-unavailable`.\n4. When the review-bot is genuinely **wedged/down** (or the mid-redeploy defer bound is exhausted), autodeploy still fails open and deploys, emitting the countable `signal-unavailable` marker — the recovery path is preserved.\n5. No capacity change (port pool / `MCP_RELEASES_CAP`) is made; both fixes are in-process/host-local (portable, no CI-provider dependency).\n6. `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the two targeted test modules pass; each mechanism has an independent RED→GREEN test.\n\n## Dedup / provenance\nPrior triage `duplicates`→6af7 was a mis-dedup (6af7 = AuthConfigError/secrets, a different deploy_failed cause) and has been corrected; `relates_to`→40a7 (the reopened design-limitation record) stands. Attribution `caused_by`→fd4a-4e91-f179-4932 (origin commit 8297083532a3) to be recorded at close. Disk bug e4f3 is a separate concurrent P2 (rejected as cause on decisive timing — see RCA comment)."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788144977972481895,"uuid":"cebd9ed6-e4b4-4401-a6ed-bb2dbabd8210"}